{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' SYMBOLS.md; printf '\\\\n--- ERRORS ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,240p' ERRORS.md; printf '\\\\n--- CONFIGS ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,260p' CONFIGS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Dynamic Symbol Surface\n\nGenerated from the default C shared library with:\n\n```text\nnm -D --defined-only --format=posix c_src/build/libdriver.so\n```\n\nThe CMake project has one shared-library target (`driver`) and no build-time\noptions. `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table, so the Rust feature matrix has\none valid combination: `--no-default-features` with an empty feature list.\n\n| C symbol | type | C source | Rust export | status |\n|----------|------|----------|-------------|--------|\n| `driver` | `T` | `c_src/src/goto.c:65` | `driver` | [ ] |\n| `forward_goto_example` | `T` | `c_src/src/goto.c:29` | `forward_goto_example` | [ ] |\n| `open_with_cleanup` | `T` | `c_src/src/goto.c:42` | `open_with_cleanup` | [ ] |\n\nThe C library's remaining dynamic symbols are undefined libc/toolchain imports,\nnot public definitions: `_ITM_deregisterTMCloneTable`,\n`_ITM_registerTMCloneTable`, `__cxa_finalize`, `__gmon_start__`, `fclose`,\n`ferror`, `fgets`, `fopen`, `fprintf`, `fwrite`, `printf`, and `stderr`.\n\nCompletion gate: [ ] the sorted C export set equals the sorted Rust export set,\nwith no missing or undefined non-libc implementation symbols.\n\n--- ERRORS ---\n# Error Surface\n\nMechanically derived from every `if` branch that returns an error or null\nsentinel in `c_src/src/goto.c`. The source contains no assertions, enums,\nlength parameters, named min/max constants, or explicit filename null check.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | verified |\n|---|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|----------|\n| 1 | `forward_goto_example` | `x < 0` (`goto error`, lines 30-31) | writes `Error: negative input\\n` to stderr and returns `-1` | [ ] |\n| 2 | `open_with_cleanup` | `fopen(filename, \"r\")` returns null (lines 43-45) | writes `Error: opening or processing file %s\\n` to stderr and returns `NULL` | [ ] |\n| 3 | `open_with_cleanup` | the read loop ends and `ferror(fp) != 0` (lines 49-54) | writes the filename error, closes `fp`, and returns `NULL` | [ ] |\n| 4 | `driver` | `forward_goto_example(num) == -1`, reached for `num < 0` (lines 66-68) | returns `-1` without opening `filename` | [ ] |\n| 5 | `driver` | `open_with_cleanup(filename) == NULL` because `fopen` failed (lines 73-75) | returns `-2` after writing the processing, goto-output, and filename-error messages | [ ] |\n| 6 | `driver` | `open_with_cleanup(filename) == NULL` because reading set `ferror` (lines 73-75) | returns `-2` after writing the processing, goto-output, and filename-error messages | [ ] |\n\nAdditional generic FFI boundaries required by Phase C:\n\n| # | function | boundary | expected parity |\n|---|----------|----------|-----------------|\n| G1 | `open_with_cleanup` | null `filename` | same process exit/signal and byte output as C; C has no explicit null rejection |\n| G2 | `driver` | `num < 0`, null `filename` | returns `-1`; the filename is not evaluated |\n| G3 | `driver` | `num >= 0`, null `filename` | same process exit/signal and byte output as C; C has no explicit null rejection |\n\nThere are no length or enum parameters, so zero/oversized lengths and invalid\nenum discriminants do not apply to this ABI.\n\n--- CONFIGS ---\n# Configuration Surface\n\n## Build-Time Matrix\n\n| # | Rust features | CMake configuration | [ ] |\n|---|---------------|----------------------|-----|\n| 1 | no features (`--no-default-features --features \"\"`) | default `driver` shared-library target; no CMake options or source `#if` branches | [ ] |\n\n## Runtime Axes\n\nThe exported ABI has no option, mode, flag, enum, length, element-type, format,\nor byte-order parameter. The C branches distinguish negative/nonnegative\nintegers, successful/failed opens, zero/one/many successful `fgets` iterations,\nand clean/error EOF. Valid integer rows also retain the zero and signed\nmultiplication-wrap boundaries because the compiled C artifact treats those\nvalue classes differently at the returned-byte level.\n\nFile shapes used below:\n\n- **empty**: readable file; zero successful `fgets` calls.\n- **one chunk**: readable nonempty file of at most 99 bytes with no earlier\n  newline; one successful `fgets` call.\n- **many chunks**: readable file causing two or more successful `fgets` calls\n  through multiple lines and/or data longer than the 99-byte payload buffer.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `forward_goto_example` | no options; `x == 0` boundary | [ ] |\n| 2 | `forward_goto_example` | no options; `1 <= x <= INT_MAX / 2`, doubled result is representable | [ ] |\n| 3 | `forward_goto_example` | no options; `INT_MAX / 2 < x <= INT_MAX`, compiled C doubled result wraps | [ ] |\n| 4 | `open_with_cleanup` | no options; readable empty file | [ ] |\n| 5 | `open_with_cleanup` | no options; readable one-chunk file | [ ] |\n| 6 | `open_with_cleanup` | no options; readable many-chunk file | [ ] |\n| 7 | `driver` | `num == 0`; readable empty file | [ ] |\n| 8 | `driver` | representable positive doubled result; readable empty file | [ ] |\n| 9 | `driver` | wrapping positive doubled result; readable empty file | [ ] |\n| 10 | `driver` | `num == 0`; readable one-chunk file | [ ] |\n| 11 | `driver` | representable positive doubled result; readable one-chunk file | [ ] |\n| 12 | `driver` | wrapping positive doubled result; readable one-chunk file | [ ] |\n| 13 | `driver` | `num == 0`; readable many-chunk file | [ ] |\n| 14 | `driver` | representable positive doubled result; readable many-chunk file | [ ] |\n| 15 | `driver` | wrapping positive doubled result; readable many-chunk file | [ ] |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
